        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF144 MediaDevices.getUserMedia() method allows resizeMode constraint]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41152</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41152"/>
        <updated>2025-09-16T04:01:37.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF144 added a new constraint parameter <code class="notranslate">resizeMode</code> for use with <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getUserMedia" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">MediaDevices.getUserMedia()</code></a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This allows a developer to specify whether the video from the camera should be cropped and/or downscaled to match other constraints, which may be natively supported by the camera - essentially gives them what they ask for rather than what the camera is capable of delivering.</p>
<p dir="auto">This adds a release note.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3417378973" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41132/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132">#41132</a></p>]]></content>
